{% set homeowner_guide %}
<p>Quick reference for Monrovia homeowners:</p>

<p><strong>Know your home's generation:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pre-1990:</strong> Likely needs full system replacement if original</li>
<li><strong>1990s-2000s:</strong> May have some life left, but watch for seam failures</li>
<li><strong>2010s-present:</strong> Builder-grade systems — watch for early problems, plan to upgrade within 10 years</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>The tree factor:</strong> Monrovia's established areas have heavy tree coverage. If you're constantly cleaning gutters:</p>
<ul>
<li>Gutter guards are worth the investment</li>
<li>Choose guards rated for your specific debris type (pine needles need different solutions than oak leaves)</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Growth-related drainage:</strong> If your property has more water issues than it used to, check what's been built uphill/upstream from you. New development changes drainage patterns. You may need to upgrade your system to handle increased runoff.</p>

<p><strong>Seasonal timing:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>March:</strong> Pre-storm season check</li>
<li><strong>November:</strong> Post-leaf drop cleaning</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>When to call:</strong></p>
